cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or programs, please cite them as below."
title: "OEIS A072503: new terms a(10)-a(400) (shoe lacings with no horizontal connections)"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kane
    family-names: Severin
    alias: kanestar2
repository-code: "https://github.com/kanestar2/oeis-a072503"
abstract: >-
  New terms a(10)..a(400) of OEIS A072503, the number of ways to lace a shoe
  with n eyelet pairs such that there is no direct horizontal connection
  between the two eyelets of a pair. Computed with Claude Code (Anthropic):
  two independent exact polynomial-time methods, written by separate AI agents,
  agree for n = 3..400; a direct subset dynamic program confirms n = 3..13 and
  literal enumeration n = 3..8. See CLAUDE_ROLE.md for who did what.
keywords:
  - OEIS
  - A072503
  - integer sequences
  - combinatorics
  - shoe lacing
  - dynamic programming
  - inclusion-exclusion
  - Claude Code
license: MIT
